# debian/source/format is '3.0 (native)', which means dpkg-source tars the
# entire working tree into the source package. docs/third_party/ holds several
# hundred megabytes of vendored upstream Proxmox git checkouts that exist only
# so a human (or `ix`) can read the code proxmod attaches to — none of it is
# built, installed or shipped.
#
# Without these two lines every `make deb` would pull that into the package.
# The second line is not redundant: tar-ignore is matched by `tar --exclude`,
# which needs the directory pattern to catch the entry itself and the wildcard
# to catch everything below it.
tar-ignore = docs/third_party
tar-ignore = docs/third_party/*
